Incredible videogame. Miraculous that beyond the immediately fascinating hand-crafted visuals and spectacular soundtrack, they managed to create such a solid and challenging game. Within the main progression and achievements, it is fair and very rewarding. The DLC content is very polished and also introduces new movement options and playstiles in the progression.

It's certainly for enjoyers of platformers and for those looking for hitless-adjacent challenges. The fun of the game is improving in the situational use of the shots and charms, getting the movement down, and learning attack patterns. Beware of the wonky default keyboard controls and the inconvenience of setting up two-player mode.

{About the hour count: I started playing on the xbox store in 2018 and have 87 hours there. Buy it on Steam; I encountered no bugs playing it here, while the other version was a bit of a headache.}

